WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.249 --> 00:00:01.208
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.208 --> 00:00:04.616
Today's message is start with a spark.

00:00:04.616 --> 00:00:05.924
Over to you Bono.

00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:07.840
(cock crows)

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.173
(rap music)

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.493
- Now when we started out,

00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:20.404
we couldn't even play our instruments.

00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:21.237
We really couldn't.

00:00:21.237 --> 00:00:24.236
We formed a band before
we could even play.

00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:27.676
And we were 16 and we didn't
know where we were going

00:00:27.676 --> 00:00:30.843
and we just decided to go there together.

00:00:30.843 --> 00:00:32.950
It was just four of us in the kitchen,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.158
in Dublin City in Ireland

00:00:35.158 --> 00:00:38.358
and Larry Mullen Junior, he's
the drummer in the group,

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:40.832
he started only, he just
kind of pinned a notice

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.936
to the notice board in school,

00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:44.191
we're starting a high school band

00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:47.829
and we got started and
actually reluctantly.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:50.355
I didn't even know if I
wanted to be in a band.

00:00:50.355 --> 00:00:53.438
And when we started to play together,

00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:57.640
when we started writing songs together,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.304
I don't know why but we felt we could,

00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:01.600
we could make a living out of it

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.412
and we felt that, it was
something special, a spark,

00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:06.867
that was different

00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:09.922
and between us and a
lot of the other bands

00:01:09.922 --> 00:01:10.755
that were starting then.

00:01:10.755 --> 00:01:11.968
We just felt we had a spark

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.896
and we started with that little spark

00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:15.832
and we've kind of fanned it a bit.

00:01:15.832 --> 00:01:16.665
Now it's a flame

00:01:16.665 --> 00:01:20.582
and I suppose a bit of
a forest fire right now.

00:01:22.298 --> 00:01:23.994
- Most people aren't happy with the spark.

00:01:23.994 --> 00:01:26.834
Most people expect instant
success as an entrepreneur.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.514
They expect that lots of
entrepreneurs have success

00:01:29.514 --> 00:01:31.029
and I'm talented and I'm smart,

00:01:31.029 --> 00:01:32.263
why can't I figure this out?

00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:34.884
And my business should work
in the first six months.

00:01:34.884 --> 00:01:36.573
I fell into the same trap.

00:01:36.573 --> 00:01:38.789
When I started my very
first company, I was 19.

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:39.697
I became an entrepreneur

00:01:39.697 --> 00:01:42.085
with my first kind of
real company I guess.

00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:44.924
I thought it would be a
lot easier than it was.

00:01:44.924 --> 00:01:47.109
I saw the articles and the magazines

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:49.276
and the shows talking about
these successful entrepreneurs

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:50.876
and I thought I can do this.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:53.129
Everything else that I had
done that I applied myself to,

00:01:53.129 --> 00:01:56.128
I had success with, so I can do this too.

00:01:56.128 --> 00:01:58.848
And I failed over and over
and over and over again

00:01:58.848 --> 00:01:59.681
and you realize

00:01:59.681 --> 00:02:01.254
and for those of you
who've been in business,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.598
you know it's way harder than
you think it's going to be.

00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:06.440
And a lot of people just quit too soon.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.875
A lot of people give up once it gets hard

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.460
because the spark isn't enough.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.610
We all have the spark

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.216
but to turn the spark into a fire,

00:02:14.216 --> 00:02:15.663
you need to work it and work it

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:17.526
and work it and work it and work it

00:02:17.526 --> 00:02:18.654
and the thing that gets you through

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:20.508
is the absolute passion
for what you're doing.

00:02:20.508 --> 00:02:22.652
If you can find the thing
that you love doing,

00:02:22.652 --> 00:02:24.827
that you would do even if you
weren't getting paid to do it,

00:02:24.827 --> 00:02:27.299
then you have to find a way to keep going.

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:28.751
Even if it doesn't make sense.

00:02:28.751 --> 00:02:30.613
Even if you've lost all practicality.

00:02:30.613 --> 00:02:31.627
Even if everybody around
you is telling you

00:02:31.627 --> 00:02:33.588
that you're crazy and stupid.

00:02:33.588 --> 00:02:35.300
If it's inside here,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.387
you have to keep finding
a way to keep going.

00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:38.787
Maybe you take on part time jobs.

00:02:38.787 --> 00:02:40.843
Maybe you go work for
somebody else, whatever it is,

00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:42.132
you have to find a way to keep going.

00:02:42.132 --> 00:02:43.938
If you've lost interest in it,

00:02:43.938 --> 00:02:45.474
it's not exciting for you anymore,

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:46.758
it was just something that you were trying

00:02:46.758 --> 00:02:47.833
to make some money off of,

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:48.761
then you should quit

00:02:48.761 --> 00:02:50.144
and move on to something else.

00:02:50.144 --> 00:02:52.394
But if you find that spark,

00:02:53.585 --> 00:02:54.777
and you think that this is something

00:02:54.777 --> 00:02:57.665
that I really, really have a
passion for and want to do,

00:02:57.665 --> 00:03:00.541
then you have to find a way to keep going,

00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:01.988
don't quit too soon

00:03:01.988 --> 00:03:04.794
and turn that spark into a fire.

00:03:04.794 --> 00:03:06.520
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.145
What's your spark?

00:03:08.145 --> 00:03:09.491
What the thing that gets you excited?

00:03:09.491 --> 00:03:10.612
What's the thing that gets you motivated?

00:03:10.612 --> 00:03:12.267
What do you love about your business?

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:13.484
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:03:13.484 --> 00:03:14.704
Super curious to find out.

00:03:14.704 --> 00:03:16.810
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to David Espejo.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:17.987
David, thank you so much

00:03:17.987 --> 00:03:20.355
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word.

00:03:20.355 --> 00:03:21.768
It really, really means a lot to me

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.208
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:24.544
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:24.544 --> 00:03:25.648
I believe in you.

00:03:25.648 --> 00:03:27.536
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:03:27.536 --> 00:03:29.433
and whatever your one word is.

00:03:29.433 --> 00:03:31.839
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:03:31.839 --> 00:03:34.178
for another Shot of Entspresoo.

00:03:34.178 --> 00:03:35.011
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:35.011 --> 00:03:38.594
