00:03:43.101 --> 00:03:43.934
- So do you have any advice

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:46.291
for someone who would like to
start doing creative writing

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:49.869
but has no idea where to start whatsoever?

00:03:49.869 --> 00:03:50.702
- [Neil] Depends.

00:03:50.702 --> 00:03:53.623
Are you the kind of person who..

00:03:53.623 --> 00:03:54.709
Do you read a lot?

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:55.857
- I read a lot, yes.

00:03:55.857 --> 00:03:57.295
And I write snarky emails

00:03:57.295 --> 00:03:59.271
but
(crowd laughs)

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.292
that's about it.
- Have

00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:01.750
- I've been told they're very good.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:02.943
- When you say creative writing,

00:04:02.943 --> 00:04:04.015
do you want to write fiction?

00:04:04.015 --> 00:04:05.833
Do you want to write humorous essays?

00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:06.666
There's an awful
- Fiction.

00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:07.499
- [Man] I would think.

00:04:07.499 --> 00:04:08.646
- You want to do stories?

00:04:08.646 --> 00:04:09.917
- Yes
- Okay.

00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:12.509
- [Neil] So my advice is
start writing stories.

00:04:12.509 --> 00:04:14.330
- Just like do it.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.954
- Really, it's almost as simple as that.

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:18.210
It's start writing, so pick a style.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.043
Pick a theme.

00:04:19.043 --> 00:04:21.323
Look at the kind of

00:04:21.323 --> 00:04:24.728
You're not expected
straight out of the hat

00:04:24.728 --> 00:04:27.831
to be a brave and original voice,

00:04:27.831 --> 00:04:29.599
producing fine and wonderful fiction.

00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:32.999
It's much more like the first pancake

00:04:32.999 --> 00:04:33.832
on the griddle,

00:04:33.832 --> 00:04:36.711
which is going to be this
weird black messy thing

00:04:36.711 --> 00:04:38.951
that you either give to
your dog or to a child.

00:04:38.951 --> 00:04:40.903
(crowd laughs)

00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:44.236
You try to convince him, yeah it's nice.

00:04:47.311 --> 00:04:48.211
You write.

00:04:48.211 --> 00:04:50.187
You finish things.

00:04:50.187 --> 00:04:51.803
You start the next thing.

00:04:51.803 --> 00:04:52.859
You write that.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.515
You finish it.

00:04:54.515 --> 00:04:58.299
Somewhere in there, you
get reasonably good.

00:04:58.299 --> 00:04:59.251
And
- Do you give these to people

00:04:59.251 --> 00:05:00.619
- [Man] Or do you just.

00:05:00.619 --> 00:05:02.131
- Yeah.

00:05:02.131 --> 00:05:06.298
The point, I always found
that I would always learn more

00:05:08.922 --> 00:05:11.466
about what I'd done the
moment I saw it in print.

00:05:11.466 --> 00:05:12.602
Or the moment, these days,

00:05:12.602 --> 00:05:15.144
probably the moment you
see things up on the web.

00:05:15.144 --> 00:05:17.208
But yeah, show 'em to people.

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:19.337
But the most important thing
when you're just starting out

00:05:19.337 --> 00:05:21.835
is write the next one.

00:05:21.835 --> 00:05:26.426
Assume that you have a
million words inside you

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.994
that are absolute rubbish

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.955
and you need to get them out

00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:31.266
before you get to the good ones.

00:05:31.266 --> 00:05:33.609
And if you get there early, that's great.

00:05:33.609 --> 00:05:35.465
That was really my biggest advice.

00:05:35.465 --> 00:05:36.298
